# Authentik providers

## Gate

Use when the user asks to list, inspect, create, or update Authentik
**providers** (OAuth2/OIDC, SAML, proxy/forward-auth, LDAP, SCIM as
exposed by the instance). Skip app-only or flow-only asks.

## Transport

No Authentik MCP discovered. Use Authentik REST API with resolved base
URL + Bearer token (never echo the token). Prefer a real Authentik MCP
later without inventing tool names.

## Resolve ids

Never invent provider `pk`, `name`, or client id. Resolve via:

| Need | API |
| --- | --- |
| All providers | `GET /api/v3/providers/all/` |
| OAuth2/OIDC | `GET /api/v3/providers/oauth2/` · `GET /api/v3/providers/oauth2/{id}/` |
| SAML | `GET /api/v3/providers/saml/` · `GET /api/v3/providers/saml/{id}/` |
| Proxy | `GET /api/v3/providers/proxy/` · `GET /api/v3/providers/proxy/{id}/` |
| Search | `?search=TERM` on the matching collection |

If the user named only a client id, search OAuth2 providers and match
`client_id` — do not guess.

## Receipt shape

Report: **name**, **type** (oauth2 / saml / proxy / …), **pk**, and for
OIDC the **client_id name only**. For SAML: ACS URL host + entity id
**names**. Never paste:

- `client_secret` / rotated secrets
- SAML signing/encryption private keys or keystores
- Proxy outpost tokens

## OIDC / OAuth2 craft (gated)

Explicit create/update verb required. Typical fields to set from the
user’s app docs (do not invent redirect URIs):

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `name` | Human label; unique enough to find later |
| `client_type` | confidential vs public — match the app |
| `redirect_uris` | Exact URIs from the RP; no wildcard guesses |
| `authorization_flow` / `invalidation_flow` | Flow pks from `authentik-flows` |
| `property_mappings` | Prefer listed mappings; do not invent UUIDs |
| `sub_mode` | Prefer stable subject modes the operator named |

| Action | API |
| --- | --- |
| Create | `POST /api/v3/providers/oauth2/` |
| Patch | `PATCH /api/v3/providers/oauth2/{id}/` |

After create, report client_id + redirect URIs. If the API returns a
client_secret, tell the operator it was issued and must land in their
secret store — **do not paste the secret into chat**. Prefer regenerating
into a store over re-display.

## SAML craft (gated)

| Action | API |
| --- | --- |
| Create | `POST /api/v3/providers/saml/` |
| Patch | `PATCH /api/v3/providers/saml/{id}/` |

Require ACS URL + audience/entity id from the SP. Do not invent NameID
maps. Never dump IdP private key PEM into chat — point at Authentik’s
download/metadata endpoints for the operator’s browser session.

## Proxy / forward-auth craft (gated)

| Action | API |
| --- | --- |
| Create | `POST /api/v3/providers/proxy/` |
| Patch | `PATCH /api/v3/providers/proxy/{id}/` |

Require external host / mode the user named. Outpost assignment and
reverse-proxy snippets are operator follow-ups — do not invent outpost
ids; list outposts when the API exposes them (`/api/v3/outposts/…`)
before binding.

## Defaults

1. List/get before mutate; prefer patch over delete+recreate.
2. Bind providers to apps via `authentik-apps` after the provider pk is
   known (see skill `authentik-sso-onboard`).
3. Authorization / invalidation flows come from `authentik-flows` — never
   invent flow pks.
4. Secret rotation and provider delete → `authentik-safety`.

## Refuse

- Inventing redirect URIs, ACS URLs, or client ids.
- Pasting client secrets, signing keys, or outpost tokens.
- Claiming a provider exists without list/get this turn.
